5e-d3a4-5eae-9540-0ee13a3dc212" :question/math-academy-id "q-108309" :question/problem "Find the intersection point of the line $l$ and the plane $Π$ with equations\n\n$$\nl:r=⟨2,3,-1⟩+t⟨-1,2,3⟩,\\,Π:r\\cdot ⟨-2,1,4⟩=11.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Let's write the equation of the line as\n\n$$\nr=⟨2-t,3+2t,-1+3t⟩.\n$$\n\nNow, substituting $r=⟨2-t,3+2t,-1+3t⟩$ into the equation of the plane, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r\\cdot ⟨-2,1,4⟩ & =11 \\\\ ⟨2-t,3+2t,-1+3t⟩\\cdot ⟨-2,1,4⟩ & =11 \\\\ -2(2-t)+1(3+2t)+4(-1+3t) & =11 \\\\ -4+2t+3+2t-4+12t & =11 \\\\ 16t & =16 \\\\ t & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, position vector $p$ of the intersection point $P$ is obtained by substituting $t=1$ into the equation of the line, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}p & =⟨2-1,3+2(1),-1+3(1)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨1,5,2⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the intersection point is $P(1,5,2).$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-108309/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "abef3da6-252e-51e4-b816-9ef7233b9a5d"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-108309"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-73985/selection/15df0ade82b8bf8f8f4944b10b21ec7a8d18a0a69205859b7224e7b7a41d168a" :answer/id #uuid "dcb7e221-c012-556f-afd1-6033b066878a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(-3,0,1)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-73985/selection/c8041c0b45c7624d574ce5092ae47ec9f4b5f3ba950a413ae68bb2ab9ecc7368" :answer/id #uuid "c3136bbc-b164-562c-8db7-072502c1a632" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "No intersection" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-73985/selection/71d46bb8af128386746fe52521e45b3fa6becded46bf21feeb047603f10d3dc7" :answer/id #uuid "43bdd26a-75ac-5fd8-9239-c7214b6e7cc0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(-13,-10,17)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-73985/selection/3aa07b1a6f3b9c81a3e2ce5715ebec5c7ebfee250742ef648fab3f84c0d3e908" :answer/id #uuid "ddc7a5c7-170d-5831-afe7-a219e769882e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(-10,-13,7)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-73985/selection/44ce8f7c1270c258ae4b69a32a56d7799b2f63db7a8dae76cd2688a19e2f18e6" :answer/id #uuid "3a165ba9-749a-5e7d-8355-e1dc9444b19e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(-17,-10,13)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-73985/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "2953b1bd-39cb-5bcf-8e0b-de035ff42ece" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-73985/selection/71d46bb8af128386746fe52521e45b3fa6becded46bf21feeb047603f10d3dc7" :answer-field/choices ["q-73985/selection/15df0ade82b8bf8f8f4944b10b21ec7a8d18a0a69205859b7224e7b7a41d168a" "q-73985/selection/c8041c0b45c7624d574ce5092ae47ec9f4b5f3ba950a413ae68bb2ab9ecc7368" "q-73985/selection/71d46bb8af128386746fe52521e45b3fa6becded46bf21feeb047603f10d3dc7" "q-73985/selection/3aa07b1a6f3b9c81a3e2ce5715ebec5c7ebfee250742ef648fab3f84c0d3e908" "q-73985/selection/44ce8f7c1270c258ae4b69a32a56d7799b2f63db7a8dae76cd2688a19e2f18e6"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-73985" :question/id #uuid "325cb2ca-450c-5da2-91d9-b7629e65e0f5" :question/math-academy-id "q-73985" :question/problem "Find the intersection point of the line $l$ and the plane $Π$ with equations\n\n$$\nl:r=⟨2,0,2⟩+t⟨3,2,-3⟩,\\,Π:r\\cdot ⟨5,-2,3⟩=6.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Let's write the equation of the line as\n\n$$\nr=⟨2+3t,2t,2-3t⟩.\n$$\n\nNow, substituting $r=⟨2+3t,2t,2-3t⟩$ into the equation of the plane, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r\\cdot ⟨5,-2,3⟩ & =6 \\\\ ⟨2+3t,2t,2-3t⟩\\cdot ⟨5,-2,3⟩ & =6 \\\\ 5(2+3t)-2(2t)+3(2-3t) & =6 \\\\ 10+15t-4t+6-9t & =6 \\\\ 2t & =-10 \\\\ t & =-5.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, position vector $p$ of the intersection point $P$ is obtained by substituting $t=-5$ into the equation of the line, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}p & =⟨2+3(-5),2(-5),2-3(-5)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-13,-10,17⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the intersection point is $P(-13,-10,17).$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-73985/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "abef3da6-252e-51e4-b816-9ef7233b9a5d"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-73985"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-108310/selection/97b73879160de69f3b23328621d9fd4b9e3ed211b28a727e6adf9649cac5845b" :answer/id #uuid "ae8eb77c-6b88-5cfe-b984-034b6b32d4bc" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(-2,3,0)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-108310/selection/3d5a38e934b8fbce3f36825fadbdb05bb4a56ff7faad9f829030b1156bf7ad93" :answer/id #uuid "98729640-d11c-57fe-b316-27485116f69d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(1,-1,1)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-108310/selection/fdba521cd1dfb7921c172d4ba999b80ad9a0b1d7a64856877a91c73248e5cd14" :answer/id #uuid "2ccb4777-a636-5447-a5d9-f3ab9b925214" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(-8,7,-2)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-108310/selection/a8383889b671fdf69177cc3a748925567f2baebfe45f3c0bd67bce7e3c49bdd6" :answer/id #uuid "136cb6b5-7e4a-5eb7-98f5-004f40e9e211" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(-5,5,-1)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-108310/selection/c8041c0b45c7624d574ce5092ae47ec9f4b5f3ba950a413ae68bb2ab9ecc7368" :answer/id #uuid "aa2791b2-66c4-5ec5-8735-1e18b0d843b9" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "No intersection" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-108310/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "cb2ddc0f-27fb-57ab-b8fc-48c5d3b48be2" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-108310/selection/fdba521cd1dfb7921c172d4ba999b80ad9a0b1d7a64856877a91c73248e5cd14" :answer-field/choices ["q-108310/selection/97b73879160de69f3b23328621d9fd4b9e3ed211b28a727e6adf9649cac5845b" "q-108310/selection/3d5a38e934b8fbce3f36825fadbdb05bb4a56ff7faad9f829030b1156bf7ad93" "q-108310/selection/fdba521cd1dfb7921c172d4ba999b80ad9a0b1d7a64856877a91c73248e5cd14" "q-108310/selection/a8383889b671fdf69177cc3a748925567f2baebfe45f3c0bd67bce7e3c49bdd6" "q-108310/selection/c8041c0b45c7624d574ce5092ae47ec9f4b5f3ba950a413ae68bb2ab9ecc7368"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-108310" :question/id #uuid "8e5fe668-3628-59a7-b261-da619f1e8497" :question/math-academy-id "q-108310" :question/problem "Find the intersection point of the line $l$ and the plane $Π$ with equations\n\n$$\nl:r=⟨-2,3,0⟩+t⟨3,-2,1⟩,\\,Π:r\\cdot ⟨4,1,-3⟩=-19.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Let's write the equation of the line as\n\n$$\nr=⟨-2+3t,3-2t,t⟩.\n$$\n\nNow, substituting $r=⟨-2+3t,3-2t,t⟩$ into the equation of the plane, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r\\cdot ⟨4,1,-3⟩ & =-19 \\\\ ⟨-2+3t,3-2t,t⟩\\cdot ⟨4,1,-3⟩ & =-19 \\\\ 4(-2+3t)+1(3-2t)-3t & =-19 \\\\ -8+12t+3-2t-3t & =-19 \\\\ 7t & =-14 \\\\ t & =-2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, position vector $p$ of the intersection point $P$ is obtained by substituting $t=-2$ into the equation of the line, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}p & =⟨-2+3(-2),3-2(-2),(-2)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-8,7,-2⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the intersection point is $P(-8,7,-2).$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-108310/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "abef3da6-252e-51e4-b816-9ef7233b9a5d"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-108310"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-108325/selection/84137bab7d8b5504c6b297eb6caf042e68fb7e0e89db4e1447795dd074a82660" :answer/id #uuid "6850bd1d-b068-5f7b-8fee-72a5ed76e4aa" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(2,-3,4)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-108325/selection/79fc1dddfc3f8003718105fbc0e20042478daef685d373a58a785223bbbd79e4" :answer/id #uuid "b6af5075-3f00-5b3e-b98d-3caab5a37adb" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(-4,-1,8)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-108325/selection/9ff4db1ee66926250b7adcdf3140657d9a51c487e7c4076947779c403ffd8683" :answer/id #uuid "23d56610-6a2a-5a66-b792-2a883a6e0483" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(5,-4,2)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-108325/selection/c8041c0b45c7624d574ce5092ae47ec9f4b5f3ba950a413ae68bb2ab9ecc7368" :answer/id #uuid "dd475f9c-5c3d-537a-a0c0-e7d3e2e12d11" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "No intersection" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-108325/selection/8fb8899aadb75cdd69c5f629750dd77b2f1cab4e7c70efc08ac756ff829ea9a0" :answer/id #uuid "9dc699a6-ddfd-5104-bda8-ad435c6ee34f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(-1,-2,6)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-108325/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "dbdd719a-4878-57c6-bcfd-7fa1eae01e15" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-108325/selection/79fc1dddfc3f8003718105fbc0e20042478daef685d373a58a785223bbbd79e4" :answer-field/choices ["q-108325/selection/84137bab7d8b5504c6b297eb6caf042e68fb7e0e89db4e1447795dd074a82660" "q-108325/selection/79fc1dddfc3f8003718105fbc0e20042478daef685d373a58a785223bbbd79e4" "q-108325/selection/9ff4db1ee66926250b7adcdf3140657d9a51c487e7c4076947779c403ffd8683" "q-108325/selection/c8041c0b45c7624d574ce5092ae47ec9f4b5f3ba950a413ae68bb2ab9ecc7368" "q-108325/selection/8fb8899aadb75cdd69c5f629750dd77b2f1cab4e7c70efc08ac756ff829ea9a0"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-108325" :question/id #uuid "5e78c76d-4b0c-5299-a8c9-57ef8fd9ba3e" :question/math-academy-id "q-108325" :question/problem "Find the intersection point of the line $l$ and the plane $Π$ with equations\n\n$$\nl:{\\begin{aligned}x=2-3t \\\\ y=-3+t \\\\ z=4+2t\\end{aligned}\\,\\text{and}\\,Π:3x+y-4z+45=0.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "We can substitute the parametric expressions for $x,$ $y,$ and $z$ of the line into the equation of the plane immediately:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3x+y-4z+45 & =0 \\\\ 3(2-3t)+(-3+t)-4(4+2t) & =-45 \\\\ 6-9t-3+t-16-8t & =-45 \\\\ -16t & =-32 \\\\ t & =2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo get the position vector $p$ of the intersection point $P$, we substitute $t=2$ into the parametric equations of the line:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x=2-3(2)=-4 \\\\ y=-3+2=-1 \\\\ z=4+2(2)=8\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the intersection point is  $P(-4,-1,8).$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-108325/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "82e761b5-ec1c-549d-b726-e0909cfe460b"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-108325"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-73999/selection/d622d25ae08442c93a180616008ec093696478b3e650ccf651195ad5860a50c0" :answer/id #uuid "01005393-fe01-5dbd-b6d9-06e68c1a5e4d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(0,3,11)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-73999/selection/8bddb4295c03dd2a58a258d02c3d0d292224e8171071e498df90f72f726e043c" :answer/id #uuid "00e01c5b-2f3c-55e8-bdde-89c15e05ec2b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(1,0,1)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-73999/selection/0f44d92b8d9e15dc10615e27aa6446a28f5a49571f0b5ef52fb8a6278d48085e" :answer/id #uuid "7315de20-0bee-54fa-a72e-d1aa9d3084e7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(10,12,11)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-73999/selection/e0d1e258f6bf6270a00ee7a2677570b2d2835f1934cb17d71d661c2ff03e6c7d" :answer/id #uuid "63885195-7515-59db-91dd-619141f62808" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(0,15,11)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-73999/selection/c8041c0b45c7624d574ce5092ae47ec9f4b5f3ba950a413ae68bb2ab9ecc7368" :answer/id #uuid "5c5047ab-818b-52c9-b2eb-3ea7c3c64f63" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "No intersection" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-73999/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "f8c4ab64-c79a-5f27-acbd-ad32ba576566" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-73999/selection/e0d1e258f6bf6270a00ee7a2677570b2d2835f1934cb17d71d661c2ff03e6c7d" :answer-field/choices ["q-73999/selection/d622d25ae08442c93a180616008ec093696478b3e650ccf651195ad5860a50c0" "q-73999/selection/8bddb4295c03dd2a58a258d02c3d0d292224e8171071e498df90f72f726e043c" "q-73999/selection/0f44d92b8d9e15dc10615e27aa6446a28f5a49571f0b5ef52fb8a6278d48085e" "q-73999/selection/e0d1e258f6bf6270a00ee7a2677570b2d2835f1934cb17d71d661c2ff03e6c7d" "q-73999/selection/c8041c0b45c7624d574ce5092ae47ec9f4b5f3ba950a413ae68bb2ab9ecc7368"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-73999" :question/id #uuid "e45ecd53-082b-51d5-8bee-c71442a1f3b8" :question/math-academy-id "q-73999" :question/problem "Find the intersection point of the line $l$ and the plane $Π$ with equations\n\n$$\nl:{\\begin{aligned}x=-2-t \\\\ y=9-3t \\\\ z=-1-6t\\end{aligned}\\,\\text{and}\\,Π:-3x+2y+5z-85=0.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "We can substitute the parametric expressions for $x,$ $y,$ and $z$ of the line into the equation of the plane immediately:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-3x+2y+5z-85 & =0 \\\\ -3(-2-t)+2(9-3t)+5(-1-6t) & =85 \\\\ 6+3t+18-6t-5-30t & =85 \\\\ -33t & =66 \\\\ t & =-2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo get the position vector $p$ of the intersection point $P$, we substitute $t=-2$ into the parametric equations of the line:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x=-2-(-2)=0 \\\\ y=9-3(-2)=15 \\\\ z=-1-6(-2)=11\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the intersection point is  $P(0,15,11).$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-73999/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "82e761b5-ec1c-549d-b726-e0909cfe460b"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-73999"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-108371/selection/d79b47437bdab0257a04aedb2610fdcfa827603e0b7f7edfd15f54f517e613fc" :answer/id #uuid "0db1fcb0-c0a8-57e5-ac80-2d73a1e639ad" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(14,-4,7)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-108371/selection/7fe53f21db7a73b99e31e6b08fa0a12532074f3353d71e785b726c59e048d73f" :answer/id #uuid "e7d6e3a2-bd17-518b-a420-9be2d6ede2d0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(9,-3,5)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-108371/selection/7feb87c90f120f336e0279405249b2c405f555a8d7fc28e1c036a2c92f7de2f9" :answer/id #uuid "fd1e7486-194c-5f91-b648-30d5fc905ddc" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(-1,-1,1)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-108371/selection/c8041c0b45c7624d574ce5092ae47ec9f4b5f3ba950a413ae68bb2ab9ecc7368" :answer/id #uuid "3142852d-48b8-5774-8470-a6efcf238212" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "No intersection" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-108371/selection/d4edf5740876051fbb03639ead5e43c7b38a5bf7e0d012bf2a8da7a66713af2e" :answer/id #uuid "bf61788e-b726-5e47-a6a7-89955c7d41db" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(-6,0,-1)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-108371/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "8269ff46-ca04-5b2b-b137-fa58cf5a3d69" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-108371/selection/d79b47437bdab0257a04aedb2610fdcfa827603e0b7f7edfd15f54f517e613fc" :answer-field/choices ["q-108371/selection/d79b47437bdab0257a04aedb2610fdcfa827603e0b7f7edfd15f54f517e613fc" "q-108371/selection/7fe53f21db7a73b99e31e6b08fa0a12532074f3353d71e785b726c59e048d73f" "q-108371/selection/7feb87c90f120f336e0279405249b2c405f555a8d7fc28e1c036a2c92f7de2f9" "q-108371/selection/c8041c0b45c7624d574ce5092ae47ec9f4b5f3ba950a413ae68bb2ab9ecc7368" "q-108371/selection/d4edf5740876051fbb03639ead5e43c7b38a5bf7e0d012bf2a8da7a66713af2e"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-108371" :question/id #uuid "0da8771f-0983-5e77-be97-afe167de38df" :question/math-academy-id "q-108371" :question/problem "Find the intersection point of the line $l$ and the plane $Π$ with equations\n\n$$\nl:r=⟨4,-2,3⟩+w⟨5,-1,2⟩,\\,Π:r=⟨10,-5,12⟩+s⟨4,3,0⟩+t⟨0,2,5⟩.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "From the equation of a plane in the parametric form $r=p+tv+sw$, we have that its normal vector is $n=v\\times w.$ In our case, the normal vector to $Π$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}n & =v\\times w \\\\  & =⟨4,3,0⟩\\times ⟨0,2,5⟩ \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 4 & 3 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 5\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}3 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 5\\end{aligned}|i-|\\begin{aligned}4 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 5\\end{aligned}|j+|\\begin{aligned}4 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 2\\end{aligned}|k \\\\  & =15i-20j+8k \\\\  & =⟨15,-20,8⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the equation of the plane $Π$ in dot product form is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r\\cdot n & =p\\cdot n \\\\ r\\cdot ⟨15,-20,8⟩ & =⟨10,-5,12⟩\\cdot ⟨15,-20,8⟩ \\\\ r\\cdot ⟨15,-20,8⟩ & =346.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, substituting $r=⟨4,-2,3⟩+w⟨5,-1,2⟩$ into the equation of the plane in dot product form, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r\\cdot ⟨15,-20,8⟩ & =346 \\\\ ⟨4+5w,-2-w,3+2w⟩\\cdot ⟨15,-20,8⟩ & =346 \\\\ 15(4+5w)-20(-2-w)+8(3+2w) & =346 \\\\ 60+75w+40+20w+24+16w & =346 \\\\ 111w & =222 \\\\ w & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, to get the position vector $q$ of the intersection point $Q,$ we substitute $w=2$ into the equation of the line:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}q & =⟨4+5(2),-2-(2),3+2(2)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨14,-4,7⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the intersection point is $Q(14,-4,7).$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-108371/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "caf29808-4551-56a0-ac86-a4587a06fc0f"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-108371"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-74004/selection/d208b5009e0053babc6220077bc016f51cdbffaec08f04255bdabdb6ac98283e" :answer/id #uuid "eeef8553-eafe-5796-8b2e-c7f2c5618cba" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(-2,-5,4)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-74004/selection/73fe555da66b6e97fe5537410b73d08d047d92d79e5bb27cd67674b805a9dc8c" :answer/id #uuid "be603d2d-d637-580d-bad6-828af604fb14" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(-5,4,2)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-74004/selection/d2dd27fcfcbfe2115a04af5707d7d8b4aa11103c35bfc29b9846ab62c6f1bf08" :answer/id #uuid "87af3ebf-4dfb-5939-8c71-f5895ce797d7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(3,1,5)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-74004/selection/c8041c0b45c7624d574ce5092ae47ec9f4b5f3ba950a413ae68bb2ab9ecc7368" :answer/id #uuid "f0252694-088c-5d76-9207-7a3057bc15fd" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "No intersection" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-74004/selection/03c224b5f5b8cfc1cf498c15b6ac29d88956c60771abaa40e583414e4280932b" :answer/id #uuid "c53a16cf-6fa4-5de2-b768-e0df5e044119" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(2,0,1)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-74004/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "6a6172fa-157e-5561-a07f-61ca4db2b67d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-74004/selection/d2dd27fcfcbfe2115a04af5707d7d8b4aa11103c35bfc29b9846ab62c6f1bf08" :answer-field/choices ["q-74004/selection/d208b5009e0053babc6220077bc016f51cdbffaec08f04255bdabdb6ac98283e" "q-74004/selection/73fe555da66b6e97fe5537410b73d08d047d92d79e5bb27cd67674b805a9dc8c" "q-74004/selection/d2dd27fcfcbfe2115a04af5707d7d8b4aa11103c35bfc29b9846ab62c6f1bf08" "q-74004/selection/c8041c0b45c7624d574ce5092ae47ec9f4b5f3ba950a413ae68bb2ab9ecc7368" "q-74004/selection/03c224b5f5b8cfc1cf498c15b6ac29d88956c60771abaa40e583414e4280932b"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-74004" :question/id #uuid "845a9150-4e19-5e0f-8a87-b8822d534204" :question/math-academy-id "q-74004" :question/problem "Find the intersection point of the line $l$ and the plane $Π$ with equations\n\n$$\nl:r=⟨3,1,5⟩+w⟨-2,-5,4⟩,\\,Π:r=⟨-5,4,2⟩+s⟨0,3,1⟩+t⟨2,0,1⟩.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "From the equation of a plane in the parametric form $r=p+tv+sw$, we have that its normal vector is $n=v\\times w.$ In our case, the normal vectors to $Π$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}n & =v\\times w \\\\  & =⟨0,3,1⟩\\times ⟨2,0,1⟩ \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 0 & 3 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}3 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}|i-|\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{aligned}|j+|\\begin{aligned}0 & 3 \\\\ 2 & 0\\end{aligned}|k \\\\  & =3i+2j-6k \\\\  & =⟨3,2,-6⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the equation of the plane $Π$ in dot product form is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r\\cdot n & =p\\cdot n \\\\ r\\cdot ⟨3,2,-6⟩ & =⟨-5,4,2⟩\\cdot ⟨3,2,-6⟩ \\\\ r\\cdot ⟨3,2,-6⟩ & =-19.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, substituting $r=⟨3,1,5⟩+w⟨-2,-5,4⟩$ into the equation of the plane in dot product form, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r\\cdot ⟨3,2,-6⟩ & =-19 \\\\ ⟨3-2w,1-5w,5+4w⟩\\cdot ⟨3,2,-6⟩ & =-19 \\\\ 3(3-2w)+2(1-5w)-6(5+4w) & =-19 \\\\ 9-6w+2-10w-30-24w & =-19 \\\\ -40w & =0 \\\\ w & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, to get the position vector $q$ of the intersection point $Q,$ we substitute $w=0$ into the equation of the line:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}q & =⟨3-2(0),1-5(0),5+4(0)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨3,1,5⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the intersection point is $Q(3,1,5).$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-74004/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "caf29808-4551-56a0-ac86-a4587a06fc0f"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-74004"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-108889/selection/a7bd32d6dee86024423821ddb974162136cefb3bb781da1e7e64f30e7cc4f98d" :answer/id #uuid "67e25cb5-4491-5247-b689-ce094bd09db1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(-7,-3,-10)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-108889/selection/5275102194955c5c5ebfedefd6454f7ee7905df637ac36c1cd5328b5698834d1" :answer/id #uuid "f70f6d86-43fd-59f7-a0fb-b400b5d7e414" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(8,3,-1)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-108889/selection/50d14f7f470e67209d480703a3372ac2e315dbaebb04e8a45aa4b07835c1954d" :answer/id #uuid "d6d831ac-92de-5fef-b4b6-09d774020b60" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(13,7,2)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-108889/selection/9b6b98e38bcc54974a36780bf7a34f113b57a413ca00f39f5b57c857d258a682" :answer/id #uuid "6fba1001-8369-5c0e-95f6-7fdb50afa8e4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(-12,-5,-13)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-108889/selection/c8041c0b45c7624d574ce5092ae47ec9f4b5f3ba950a413ae68bb2ab9ecc7368" :answer/id #uuid "0380037d-3624-5985-af69-76df39ab115c" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "No intersection" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-108889/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "46fdd381-d1f3-5a54-b9a2-08fb1c4a79c0" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-108889/selection/9b6b98e38bcc54974a36780bf7a34f113b57a413ca00f39f5b57c857d258a682" :answer-field/choices ["q-108889/selection/a7bd32d6dee86024423821ddb974162136cefb3bb781da1e7e64f30e7cc4f98d" "q-108889/selection/5275102194955c5c5ebfedefd6454f7ee7905df637ac36c1cd5328b5698834d1" "q-108889/selection/50d14f7f470e67209d480703a3372ac2e315dbaebb04e8a45aa4b07835c1954d" "q-108889/selection/9b6b98e38bcc54974a36780bf7a34f113b57a413ca00f39f5b57c857d258a682" "q-108889/selection/c8041c0b45c7624d574ce5092ae47ec9f4b5f3ba950a413ae68bb2ab9ecc7368"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-108889" :question/id #uuid "2d225520-d7e9-5a28-afbf-6e16563a3611" :question/math-academy-id "q-108889" :question/problem "Find the intersection point of the line $l$ and the plane $Π$ with equations\n\n$$\nl:\\frac{x-3}{5}=\\frac{y-1}{2}=\\frac{z+4}{3},\\,Π:r\\cdot ⟨-3,2,-1⟩=39.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "From the equation of the line $l$, we know that it passes through the point $A(3,1,-4)$ and it is parallel to the vector $v=⟨5,2,3⟩.$ Therefore, its vector equation is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r & =⟨3,1,-4⟩+t⟨5,2,3⟩ \\\\  & =⟨3+5t,1+2t,-4+3t⟩,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).$\n\nNow, substituting $r=⟨3+5t,1+2t,-4+3t⟩$ into the equation of the plane, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r\\cdot ⟨-3,2,-1⟩ & =39 \\\\ ⟨3+5t,1+2t,-4+3t⟩\\cdot ⟨-3,2,-1⟩ & =39 \\\\ (-3)(3+5t)+2(1+2t)-(-4+3t) & =39 \\\\ -9-15t+2+4t+4-3t & =39 \\\\ -14t & =42 \\\\ t & =-3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, to get the position vector $p$ of the intersection point $P,$ we substitute $t=-3$ into the equation of the line:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}p & =⟨3+5(-3),1+2(-3),-4+3(-3)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-12,-5,-13⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we get $P(-12,-5,-13).$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-108889/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "caf29808-4551-56a0-ac86-a4587a06fc0f"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-108889"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-33081"] :question/problem "Find the intersection point of the line $l$ and the plane $Π$ with equations\n\n$$\nl:\\frac{x-1}{2}=\\frac{y+2}{1}=\\frac{z-1}{3},\\,Π:r\\cdot ⟨1,6,2⟩=19.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "From the equation of the line $l$, we know that it passes through the point $A(1,-2,1)$ and it is parallel to the vector $v=⟨2,1,3⟩.$ Therefore, its vector equation is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r & =⟨1,-2,1⟩+t⟨2,1,3⟩ \\\\  & =⟨1+2t,-2+t,1+3t⟩,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).$\n\nNow, substituting $r=⟨1+2t,-2+t,1+3t⟩$ into the equation of the plane, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r\\cdot ⟨1,6,2⟩ & =19 \\\\ ⟨1+2t,-2+t,1+3t⟩\\cdot ⟨1,6,2⟩ & =19 \\\\ (1+2t)+6(-2+t)+2(1+3t) & =19 \\\\ 1+2t-12+6t+2+6t & =19 \\\\ 14t & =28 \\\\ t & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, to get the position vector $p$ of the intersection point $P,$ we substitute $t=2$ into the equation of the line:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}p & =⟨1+2(2),-2+2,1+3(2)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨5,0,7⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we get $P(5,0,7).$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "q-33197/selection/c018a25cb2ecc6ccbd1a6f5544f028ac0a2809bbc4d5d2079ba74edc42af2d5d" :answer/id #uuid "5f32b3e5-ada1-5833-bda5-8c4236ce226b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(-3,2,-1)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-33197/selection/c8041c0b45c7624d574ce5092ae47ec9f4b5f3ba950a413ae68bb2ab9ecc7368" :answer/id #uuid "60d6d238-7b70-5c55-af31-e93aac243f58" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "No intersection" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-33197/selection/fb7a7c474ff6a4155588236dcee8c90d52241e4de6e0f1d16b3c94e7734ebf87" :answer/id #uuid "59d9b629-b554-58d8-8bb5-35a5aca1c3db" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(11,-3,-1)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-33197/selection/7c777b3895066f9fa230ae68e1c6ea601a73169ac7019d03fc512ff6f9a747ad" :answer/id #uuid "f0b88eff-8ed7-5763-8342-49fe491b68cf" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(1,-3,-11)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-33197/selection/942c6b6ce410ed5f547cb5876cd8e598dfb4001dfbace67cc2fd140b4e164094" :answer/id #uuid "719be12e-1496-55f2-b6c2-e488693d6fe8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(11,-1,-3)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-33197/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "c8ac8054-65d2-5274-b462-4accb5725bdc" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-33197/selection/fb7a7c474ff6a4155588236dcee8c90d52241e4de6e0f1d16b3c94e7734ebf87" :answer-field/choices ["q-33197/selection/c018a25cb2ecc6ccbd1a6f5544f028ac0a2809bbc4d5d2079ba74edc42af2d5d" "q-33197/selection/c8041c0b45c7624d574ce5092ae47ec9f4b5f3ba950a413ae68bb2ab9ecc7368" "q-33197/selection/fb7a7c474ff6a4155588236dcee8c90d52241e4de6e0f1d16b3c94e7734ebf87" "q-33197/selection/7c777b3895066f9fa230ae68e1c6ea601a73169ac7019d03fc512ff6f9a747ad" "q-33197/selection/942c6b6ce410ed5f547cb5876cd8e598dfb4001dfbace67cc2fd140b4e164094"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-33197" :question/id #uuid "f5c58476-2e22-55a5-af93-3aace6df8e02" :question/math-academy-id "q-33197" :question/problem "Find the intersection point of the line $l$ and the plane $Π$ with equations\n\n$$\nl:\\frac{x-2}{-3}=\\frac{y-3}{2}=\\frac{z+4}{-1},\\,Π:3x-2y+z-38=0.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "From the equation of the line $l$, we know that it passes through the point $A(2,3,-4)$ and it is parallel to the vector $v=⟨-3,2,-1⟩.$ Therefore, its parametric equations are given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r & =⟨2,3,-4⟩+t⟨-3,2,-1⟩ \\\\  & =⟨2-3t,3+2t,-4-t⟩,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).$\n\nLet's also write the equation of the plane in the dot product form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3x-2y+z-38 & =0 \\\\ 3x-2y+z & =38 \\\\ ⟨x,y,z⟩\\cdot ⟨3,-2,1⟩ & =38 \\\\ r\\cdot ⟨3,-2,1⟩ & =38\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, substituting $r=⟨2-3t,3+2t,-4-t⟩$ into the equation of the plane, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r\\cdot ⟨3,-2,1⟩ & =38 \\\\ ⟨2-3t,3+2t,-4-t⟩\\cdot ⟨3,-2,1⟩ & =38 \\\\ 3(2-3t)-2(3+2t)+(-4-t) & =38 \\\\ 6-9t-6-4t-4-t & =38 \\\\ -14t & =42 \\\\ t & =-3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, to get the position vector $p$ of the intersection point $P,$ we substitute $t=-3$ into the vector equation of the line:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}p & =⟨2-3(-3),3+2(-3),-4-(-3)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨11,-3,-1⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we get $P(11,-3,-1).$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-33197/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "caf29808-4551-56a0-ac86-a4587a06fc0f"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-33197"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "e-4945"] :question/problem "Find the intersection point of the line $l$ and the plane $\\Pi$ with equations\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14083348/assets/2989739b62112c05f49beb975eb9039d1bbc7fca39ffd4d0adc058c7cf1cbb41.png)" :db/ensure [:question/validate]}]
